==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|goh|loup}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*laubą}}, perhaps from {{der|de|ine-pro|*lewbʰ-|id=cut off|t=peel, break off}}.<ref>''[https://web.archive.org/web/20190330125056/https://www.hmhco.com/shop/books/The-American-Heritage-Dictionary-of-IndoEuropean-Roots-Third-Edition/9780547549446 The American Heritage Dictionary of Indo-European Roots, Third Edition]''</ref> Compare {{cog|nds|Loov}}, {{cog|nl|loof}}, {{cog|en|leaf}}, {{cog|da|løv}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/laʊ̯p/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Laub.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|de|aʊ̯p|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n,(e)s.sg}}

# {{lb|de|collective}} [[foliage]], [[greenery]], [[leaves]] {{gloss|on a tree or fallen onto the ground, but particularly the latter}}
#: {{uxi|de|grünes '''Laub'''|green foliage}}
#: {{uxi|de|fallendes '''Laub'''|falling foliage}}
#* {{quote-book|de|author=Hans Wollschläger|year=1984|title=Von Sternen und Schnuppen: bei Gelegenheit einiger Bücher|volume=1|page=209|text=Sie [die Orangen] hängen eben tatsächlich mitten im grünen '''Laub''' gelb an den Bäumen.|t=They [the oranges] indeed are right now hanging amidst green foliage at the trees.}}
# [[leaves]], a [[suit]] in [[German playing cards]]

